WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.520
The first preliminaries of the Monaco Cup have started.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.050
In this preliminary round,

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.950
bread could only be made using the ingredients acquired via the roulette.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:18.500
It’s eggs!

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.160
We got eggs!

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:25.540
I’m good with aiming lightly for either
salt or sugar, which have the greatest odds.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.140
Now, just watch!

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.050
Suwabara style’s ultimate technique:

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.060
Dragon at the Summit!

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:42.640
So close...

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:43.770
You’re a moron!

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.980
The Japanese representatives ended up acquiring only eggs,

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.150
and were in a desperate situation.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:51.860
However, from Kazuma’s suggestion,

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.110
they made a bread without using salt or sugar.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.740
With <i>Japan</i> #21, they faced the challenge.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.240
All right then, judging begins!

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:03.500
Moving quickly, moving quickly!

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.460
No! No! No!

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.960
Chile, Mongolia, and Russia’s breads get 0 points.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.170
How can you say that?

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.170
How can you give 0 points without tasting it?!

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:14.140
Because I am a clown!

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.930
Azuma-kun, are we really all right?!

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:23.270
It’s finally going to start.

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:32.440
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.360
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.570
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.970
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:39.970 --> 00:01:45.250
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:45.250 --> 00:01:48.540
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.720
Snacks at 3 p.m.!!

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:24.430
It’s <i>Japan</i> #21!

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.190
I will begin the scoring...

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.780
of this bread, which has neither salt nor sugar in it.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:46.030
There’s no need to get all that nervous.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:50.410
I know that you’ve applied a trick to the
bread, since it has neither sugar nor salt in it.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:54.540
I will not give you 0 points without even trying it, like I did with the Russian representatives.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:58.920
But...

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.470
It’s a bread with an unusual shape.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.720
What’s it called?

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:05.470
That’s <i>Japan</i> #21...

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:07.470
The Castella <i>Japan</i>!

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.060
You mean that this bread is like a castella, right?

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:15.780
Well, it’s like a castella in terms of
having eggs and flour as ingredients.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.770
But, to think it’s a castella...

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.610
Hey, old... I mean handsome-and-cool Mister Pierrot...

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.530
Eat it quickly, or it’ll get cold.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:26.990
Hmm, yes...

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.250
Well then...

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:34.500
Chomp.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:35.920
He ate it!

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.090
This man can create up to 135 copies of himself

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:41.170
using a cloning technique that’s at the world level...

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:43.010
So, what kind of reaction will he show?!

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:44.010
Wait!

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:44.630
There, there.
Wait!

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:45.090
There, there.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.520
My name is Pierrot Bolneze.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:58.520
I was born as a “lost item” in the
Quedam Circus, which traveled the world.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:01.230
Another day, another performance ended safely.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.070
Don Jancour
Another day, another performance ended safely.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.530
Don Jancour

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:04.820
Boss!

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:05.990
We have a problem!

00:05:08.280 --> 00:05:09.330
What’s wrong?

00:05:09.330 --> 00:05:12.540
T-There’s a lost item in one of the audience seats.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.040
Lost item?

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.790
That was... me.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:20.800
Oh... a baby?

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.300
To forget their child...

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.180
My parents must have been really forgetful.

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.510
What should we do with this child?

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:29.850
Hmm...

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.100
I’m sure that the boss was
unsure himself, in the beginning...

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:34.520
However...

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.270
All right, let’s keep this child.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.770
His name will be...

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.070
Let’s see...

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:44.400
Pierrot...

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:47.280
Bolneze.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:48.780
It will be Pierrot Bolneze.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.490
Bolneze was the name of a designer of clown’s clothing.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:59.750
In this manner, I came to
carry a new fate as Pierrot Bolneze.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.960
Don’t be afraid, Bolneze.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:07.380
That’s right.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.800
Let go of his hands over there.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:11.510
That’s good.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:12.890
That’s good, Bolneze!

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.020
Listen up, Bolneze.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.650
The truth is that the most amazing
performer in a circus is the clown.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.860
In any circus, in order to become the clown,

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:35.040
you must be a first class performer with
mastery over all aspects of the circus,

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.540
including the trapeze, ball balancing,
acrobatics and animal training.

00:06:39.420 --> 00:06:44.210
If you become that great of a performer,
I’m sure that your parents will come to get you.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:45.050
Really?

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.050
Of course.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:51.300
The legendary clown of France, Arezzo,

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.800
worked out unparalleled performances on the trapeze,

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:55.890
with ball balancing and various other acts.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:07:01.060
They say that he could attract
thousands of people to come, all by himself.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:11.110
If you become a clown who
can attract that large an audience,

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:13.570
someday, your papa and mama are sure to...

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:15.870
That’s right!

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.290
I’ll do it...

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.830
I’ll become a legendary clown!

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:20.830
In this manner,

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.710
in order to become a legendary clown...

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:27.050
day after day, I continued to practice.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:34.840
Before I realized it, I had
become a fully qualified clown.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.550
That’s amazing, Bolneze!

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.100
At that time, Quedam was still largely unknown.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:47.820
However, my performances had begun to
have a small, but steady, group of fans.

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.030
How much longer will this story go on?

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:56.870
I really didn’t think he’d start from when he was a baby!

00:07:56.870 --> 00:08:00.290
All the other representatives have received
their scores from his clones and gone home.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:05.120
After him having talked for all this time,
I’ve yet to hear the “c” of castella.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:08.460
And more than anything else, I can’t
bear the fact that all of the 135 clones,

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:10.550
who’ve finished their scoring, are all talking at once.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:13.010
Be quiet and listen.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:15.010
We can’t afford to lose any more points.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.600
We’re going to Japan?!

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:23.890
Is that for real, Boss?

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:25.480
Yeah.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:29.190
The Saltimpanco Circus, which went
to Japan last year, was really popular.

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:31.400
It seems that their ticket sales
were in the hundreds of millions.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.280
H-Hundreds of millions?!

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:34.610
That’s amazing...

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.740
But, Boss...

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.410
While Japan may be profitable,

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.780
the overhead there will be very high.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:43.620
The cost of the site for the tent and
everything else will be ridiculously high.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:48.250
The Saltimpanco Circus did well because they had Japanese television backing them.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.630
But, we won’t have that...

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.960
Should the show fail...

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.090
Quedam would definitely be crushed.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:59.680
If there exists a possibility for profit,
we’ll go to any country for it.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:01.600
That’s what Quedam is, right?

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:02.650
But...!

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.100
And...

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:09.110
Before I leave, the last thing that I want
to do is to make Quedam bigger.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:11.360
L-Last thing?

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:15.610
I’ll retire after the show in Japan.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:17.570
Quedam will then be yours.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:18.860
Boss...

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:20.870
I’ll leave it to you.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:22.620
You’re a clown.

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:25.830
Be sure to study Japanese properly, too.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:27.750
Very well.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:35.100
In this manner, we came to Japan, but...

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:42.370
Things turned out as we had expected.

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:45.310
We had no announcements on television.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:49.600
A foreign circus coming in suddenly to
perform couldn’t possibly have done well.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.650
The bills for the tent site...

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:55.980
and food bills for the circus performers and animals...

00:09:56.610 --> 00:10:00.080
We were really suffering because
of the high cost of living in Japan.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.990
It’s no good.

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:02.820
Quedam can’t...

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.660
If only we had a legendary clown...

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.170
A legendary clown...

00:10:12.210 --> 00:10:13.750
At that time,

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:16.070
the legendary clown had come up with tricks that nobody had seen before,

00:10:16.070 --> 00:10:17.660
thus gaining great popularity.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:23.850
That’s right!

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.680
I should become the legendary clown.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.390
A new trick...

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:30.440
But...

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:34.810
What kind of trick would be
welcomed by the Japanese...?

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.750
It’s already three in the afternoon.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.660
It was time for three o’clock snacks!

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.740
The moment I glanced at and saw that ad...

00:10:46.740 --> 00:10:50.000
I felt an impact, like electricity running down my back.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:11.110
T-This is it!

00:11:12.140 --> 00:11:16.730
Thanks to that “castella something,
telephone something” ad,

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.940
I came up with my cloning trick,

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.900
and both Quedam and I became world famous!

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:29.700
Although there remains one
thing that has not changed...

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:30.620
That is...

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:34.250
Even now, I am a “lost item.”

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:39.000
But, I will not give up! I can’t give up!

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.840
This Castella <i>Japan</i> has given me
that kind of confidence once again.

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:45.440
Thank you, Japan!

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:47.180
5 points!

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:48.350
You have full marks!

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:56.690
Oh...?

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.950
I guess that was to be expected.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.370
It’s three o’clock in the morning.

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:19.920
Look, Edward.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:22.470
The Japanese representatives got full points, after all.

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:24.850
We were right in staying behind.

00:12:24.850 --> 00:12:27.470
Yeah, but I don’t understand it.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.550
In addition to eggs and flour,

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:33.100
a castella must have plenty of sugar in it.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:38.480
How could the Japanese representatives have made it if they hadn’t acquired any sugar?

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.980
They had plenty of sugar.

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:41.480
What?

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.990
Do you know what flour they chose?

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:46.780
N-No.

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:48.500
It was hatsuga genbaku flour.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.830
Hatsuga genbaku flour?

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:53.080
When wheat begins to germinate,

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:55.080
it secretes high levels of sugar.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:59.080
When you grind it into flour just like that,

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:00.880
you get hatsuga genbaku flour.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.840
As expected, you can make something
sweet with it, without using any sugar.

00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:07.350
S-Such a flour is...

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:11.680
With this, we know for sure that
this year, Japan is a serious enemy.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.430
I guess crushing them quickly would be for the best...

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:16.600
Don’t you think so, Brother?

00:13:18.390 --> 00:13:19.190
Brother?

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:22.730
Brother...

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:24.700
you were sleeping, weren’t you?

00:13:26.320 --> 00:13:28.740
No, I was kidding!

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.410
Brother, you weren’t sleeping!

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.370
You weren’t sleeping...

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.030
Ah, please stop!

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:34.240
Exactly what kind of attack is happening inside...?
Ah, please stop!

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:35.960
Exactly what kind of attack is happening inside...?

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:44.710
By the way, the castella
didn’t originate in Japan, Azuma...

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.380
You’re kidding again...

00:13:58.930 --> 00:14:00.940
Wow, that’s amazing!

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:05.440
Azuma and the others seem to have passed
the first preliminaries with the full 5 points.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:09.030
Their points have gone up from -2 to +3.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:09.950
They did it!

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:13.030
However, the preliminaries are not over yet.

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:14.950
The hard part will probably begin now.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:17.290
I... guess.

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:19.910
The hard part?

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:21.040
Like you have the right to say that.

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:23.210
Do you know what you’d truly call hard...?

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:25.960
Thank you very much.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:27.300
There.

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.300
<i>This</i> is what you call hard!

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:34.550
You all did really well.

00:14:34.550 --> 00:14:37.260
Yeah, but we can’t relax yet.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.930
Last year, among the 16 countries
that passed the preliminaries,

00:14:39.930 --> 00:14:42.060
the lowest score was a 7.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:45.770
This year, we can also expect it to be at that level.

00:14:45.770 --> 00:14:49.570
In the second preliminary,
Japan has to get at least 4 points.

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:53.200
With our losing 2 points, it was just right.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:57.040
With the extra 2 points there, it would’ve been so easy, we would’ve lost our will to try.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.990
Don’t justify your mistake, Baldy.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:00.790
What was that?!

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:04.830
Either way, Azuma, you did really well.

00:15:04.830 --> 00:15:08.460
Although, I’m really impressed that
you knew about hatsuga genbaku flour.

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:09.750
Oh, regarding that...

00:15:09.760 --> 00:15:13.840
In the finals of the newcomers’ battle,
Kanmuri had used a special flour, right?

00:15:13.840 --> 00:15:15.220
At that time...

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:18.720
I realized there are various kinds of
flour, and I should know about them.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:22.980
So, I had a wheat-farmer friend in the
neighborhood teach me various things...

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:23.810
That’s why I knew about it.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:27.190
Wow, you’re really knowledgeable, Sayo-chan.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:31.860
So, since <i>Japan</i> #21 was
originally made with sugar and eggs...

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:35.360
I thought we could use that instead of sugar to make it.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:36.910
I see.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:39.450
Even after winning against
Kanmuri, instead of being self-satisfied,

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:42.160
you take an attitude of trying to
master the way of the bread even further...

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:43.910
That’s impressive, Azuma.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:45.580
Really, completely different from Baldy.

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:46.420
I’m <i>not</i> bald!

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:50.670
However, I’ve also grown after being beaten by you.

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.880
I’m no longer the person I was before.

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:54.970
Next time, it’s my turn.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:56.340
Remember that.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:15:59.390
Suwabara...?

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.770
He sure is a guy with a lot of pride.

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:09.480
In the first preliminary, he just
depended on you and merely helped you out.

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:11.400
I’m sure he’s unsatisfied with just that.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.400
Oh well, don’t worry about it.

00:16:20.070 --> 00:16:22.910
I aim for the highest peak that a baker can reach.

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:24.870
Therefore, at this competition,

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:28.420
I must defeat as many veterans
of the world as possible myself.

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:32.540
However, as long as it’s a team match,

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.670
I can’t fight with the veterans without surpassing you.

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:37.920
If things stay like this, then next time will also...

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:40.140
It’s <i>Japan</i> number “that one”!

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:43.930
That’s what you’ll tell us, and I’ll just become a helper to you.

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:47.270
Just watch, Azuma.

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:51.520
The next preliminary is where
I’ll show you my true power!

00:16:56.740 --> 00:16:59.660
The next day

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:05.200
Well then,

00:17:05.200 --> 00:17:07.000
let’s give it all we have today, too!

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:07.540
Yeah!

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:10.120
Good morning, Japanese representatives.

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.790
The first preliminary was spectacular.

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:14.670
Kayser...

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.090
Ah, it’s the one-tiered guy!

00:17:16.460 --> 00:17:17.590
What do you want?

00:17:18.050 --> 00:17:19.130
No, you see...

00:17:19.130 --> 00:17:21.680
Since you were truly spectacular,

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:24.850
a fire was lit within our artisan souls.

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:26.600
A bet, you say?!

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:27.810
Yes.

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:30.350
In the next preliminary, between Japan and France.

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:33.570
A bet where the side with fewer points will leave.

00:17:34.020 --> 00:17:35.400
Don’t talk nonsense.

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:38.110
There’s nothing for us to gain
from doing something like that.

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:40.320
Of course there is.

00:17:40.320 --> 00:17:43.320
That is, if you truly intend to win.

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:49.080
We are the top seed for the
championship, and thus are in your way.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:52.580
By defeating us quickly,
wouldn’t you be able to relax?

00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:56.250
Also, as a handicap, only I, the third
brother, will be the French representative.

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:59.510
Only I, Edward, will take you on.

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:02.590
We promise that the older brothers will not help at all.

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:04.300
Oh...?

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.260
Hey, what was that?!

00:18:06.260 --> 00:18:08.010
Taking us on by yourself...

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.810
You’re underestimating us quite a lot!

00:18:10.640 --> 00:18:12.980
...is what I’m saying,
but it might be a pretty good deal.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.350
But Suwabara’s personality
won’t let him accept it...

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.400
and I have my pride, too...

00:18:17.400 --> 00:18:18.820
So, I should get mad over here.

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:21.570
So, you tell them off too, Suwabara.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.070
I accept that bet.

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:24.320
Uh...

00:18:24.320 --> 00:18:25.360
However...

00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:28.280
It shall be without the handicap.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:30.660
If there’s only one of you,
then there shall only be one of us.

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:32.330
I’ll take you on by myself.

00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.210
Wait!

00:18:34.210 --> 00:18:35.420
Without a handicap?!

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:36.800
Are you sure?

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:43.260
If you’re not careful about how you
use your pride, you’ll burn yourself.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:45.300
Better than letting it rust.

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:48.180
Don’t regret it.

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:51.270
That goes for you, too.

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.480
Moron!

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:57.940
What are you going to do, now
that you’ve made that promise?!

00:18:57.940 --> 00:19:00.940
We don’t really know their true strength yet!

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:03.320
You even wasted the handicap they gave us!

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:05.360
“Better than letting it rust,” you say?!

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.160
Feed your pride to the damn dog or something!

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:09.030
Shut it.

00:19:09.030 --> 00:19:12.500
Should you wail any more than that,
I’ll make you the rust on my sword.

00:19:14.790 --> 00:19:16.420
You say something, too, Azuma.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:19.840
Weren’t you also mad about the
handicap France gave us earlier?

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:23.960
You know, adults often say one thing when
they’re thinking something entirely different...

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:24.840
I...

00:19:27.050 --> 00:19:28.550
really won’t do anything.

00:19:29.720 --> 00:19:30.600
I’m grateful.

00:19:33.060 --> 00:19:34.810
A-Azuma-kun...

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:36.390
All right, from here,

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:40.110
we will now begin the ingredient slot
machines for the second preliminary round.

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.820
Just one representative from each
country sit at the slot machine, please.

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:54.450
I don’t know what karma we have
for things to have turned out like this...

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:57.710
Is it really all right to leave things to just Suwabara?

00:19:58.370 --> 00:20:00.210
He’s scary if he’s an enemy, but...

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.880
He’s really dependable if he’s on your side...

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:05.220
Suwabara, that is.

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:08.220
Well, that might be true, but...

00:20:11.930 --> 00:20:14.850
The first preliminary was roulette,
and the second is slot machines, eh?

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:16.230
How inelegant.

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:25.360
Over there!

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:36.620
A mere slot machine is no opponent for
me, a person who has mastered the sword.

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:39.210
I can see the pictures on the
drums as if they weren’t moving at all.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:41.800
I see it, I can see it!

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:43.500
I can see the timing!

00:20:44.750 --> 00:20:46.750
One. Two. Three.

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:22.750
The coins are gushing forth with terrific intensity.

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:23.540
Amazing!

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:27.710
Oh, you’ve gotten quite a lot, haven’t you?

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:29.550
You seem to be good at the slot machines.

00:21:33.340 --> 00:21:36.260
You seem to be terribly terrible at the slot machine.

00:21:36.260 --> 00:21:37.260
Well, hang in there.

00:21:37.260 --> 00:21:41.640
Being too greedy does not lead to anything good.

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:45.350
Well then,

00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:48.110
since all of you have gotten your coins...

00:21:48.110 --> 00:21:51.110
I will explain the rules for the second preliminary.

00:21:51.860 --> 00:21:56.370
There seem to have been people who got tons
and tons of coins, and some who didn’t get many.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:22:01.950
The coins you hold have various
ingredients written on them, right?

00:22:04.370 --> 00:22:09.960
This time, all of the ingredients that are
on the coins which you have acquired...

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:15.010
<i>must</i> be used to make a single bread.

00:22:15.010 --> 00:22:17.550
If there is even a single unused ingredient...

00:22:17.550 --> 00:22:19.190
You will be immediately disqualified.

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:21.680
All of the ingredients?!

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:27.520
Farewell, Japanese representative.

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:07.000
What was that?!

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:11.000
Making a single bread using all of
these ingredients is absolutely impossible!

00:24:11.000 --> 00:24:11.750
Impossible times two!

00:24:11.750 --> 00:24:12.790
Oh, shut up.

00:24:12.790 --> 00:24:14.130
Shut up and watch.

00:24:14.590 --> 00:24:15.720
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.720 --> 00:24:16.900
<i>Lupan</i> #3!!

00:24:16.900 --> 00:24:18.550
Pan d’épice, Kai-style(Kai)!
Note: The first “Kai” (<b>戒) refers to Suwabara’s name.
The second “kai” (改) means “reborn.”</b>

00:24:18.550 --> 00:24:19.380
Be sure to watch!
Note: The first “Kai” (<b>戒) refers to Suwabara’s name.
The second “kai” (改) means “reborn.”</b>

00:24:19.380 --> 00:24:19.900
Note: The first “Kai” (<b>戒) refers to Suwabara’s name.
The second “kai” (改) means “reborn.”</b>

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:22.640
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:23.140 --> 00:24:24.600
The sweet and delicious castella.

00:24:24.600 --> 00:24:26.920
Originally, it had been called biscotto,

00:24:26.920 --> 00:24:29.270
but since it originated from the Castile region of Spain,

00:24:29.270 --> 00:24:31.670
the Japanese began to call it “castella.”

00:24:32.190 --> 00:24:33.520
Really?!
